      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed with jobredeaux@:\n\nI made some changes to address this, but the simpler way of handling exports now causes java_plugin to complain because it also does not support an exports attribute. Unlike, android_app, java_plugin probably needs to \"export\" its static_libs dependencies because there will be upstream modules which depend on it.\n\nI\u0027m going to see if we can write a macro that converts java_plugins to a java_library that with the `exported_plugin` attribute to export the plugin, and a separate `exports` attribute to exports the static libs. Romain found some code in google3 that does just this, but we will have to see if the host-compatibility attributes of java_plugins throws any wrenches in this solution.",
